--- !u!114 &1753929911
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1753929908}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8d5be57ef61e14ff39321ed63a581266, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: AudioFeatureLab::AudioFeatureLab.DemoOverlay
  title: 'AudioSource: 2D and 3D'
  body: 'Walk with WASD. Click the view, then look with the mouse. Shift runs. Esc
    unlocks the cursor.


    The cyan sphere is 2D (spatial blend 0). It stays in
    both speakers as you walk.

    The orange beacon is 3D. It pans and falls off
    with distance. Green and orange rings are min and max distance.

    The yellow
    hybrid source is the settings lab. B cycles 2D, 3D, and hybrid. R cycles rolloff.
    V toggles spread.

    Select Hybrid Source and watch spatialBlend, dopplerLevel,
    spread, minDistance, maxDistance, and priority.


    The moving cube is a Doppler
    shuttle. Stand still and let it pass. Its velocity update mode is Dynamic, so
    a moving transform (no Rigidbody) still shifts pitch.

    The purple source
    sits behind the wall. The wall is on the AudioOcclusion layer. OcclusionLowPass
    raycasts only that layer, so the player and other objects are not barriers. Walk
    around the wall.

    The green disc is an AudioReverbZone using the Cave preset.
    Step inside it.

    Space plays a footstep from OneShotPool at your feet.


    M
    menu. P pauses every voice (AudioListener.pause). [ and ] change AudioListener.volume.

    Click
    the Game view so the editor does not take the keys.'
  scroll: {x: 0, y: 0}
  width: 520
